<Page social="0" voiceTypeId="0">*cough* *cough* This is an old Shurian building.</Page>
<Page social="0" voiceTypeId="0">*cough* Balderon was a place where the knowledge of the Baraka was kept. There doesn't seem to be much left.</Page>
<Page social="0" voiceTypeId="0">....</Page>
<Page social="0" voiceTypeId="0">10093 Fishing Association Executive</Page>
<Page social="0" voiceTypeId="0">A convenient way to travel between hunting areas.</Page>
<Page social="0" voiceTypeId="0">A convenient way to travel between hunting areas.</Page>
<Page social="0" voiceTypeId="0">A convenient way to travel between hunting areas.</Page>
<Page social="0" voiceTypeId="0">A huge change is coming.</Page>
<Page social="0" voiceTypeId="0">A strange place where argons and demokrons gather.</Page>
<Page social="0" voiceTypeId="0">After Balder's death, many Baraka vowed to tread a new path. Although many stayed in Southern Shara to rebuild, many instead voyaged to Southern Arun in search of new hope. Here, they established a new city: "Baldereon"─ created on the basis of advancing knowledge and maintaining peace. The Baraka of Balderon wished to pave a new path and leave the history of the Eclipse Tribe behind them.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;Over time, they became known for their willingness to share their knowledge gained throughout the centuries. They helped pave the way to new medical procedures, such as reducing the usage of bandages in favor of more potent draughts and elixirs. Shortly after Balderon's inception, the Baraka there became known as advisors, healers and mentors to those in need.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;Anyone willing to walk the new path of Balder─ one of peace and guidance─ were allowed access to Baldera. The Baraka overlooked the past of those who wished to turn over a new leaf; remembering their own roots. As the chaos that enveloped Arborea loomed and grew, a barrier formed around Baldera. This barrier protected them from the Argons, the civil war between the Alliances and even Demokrons from the north years later.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;After the Federation put an end to the Alliances, the Mysterium was contracted to investigate the great barrier. Ryshan, the lead arcanist, determined that it was made with ancient Elven magic lost to history. The only time anyone saw a glimpse into Baldera was in the sky through Sky Cruiser Intrepid while on its voyage to Northern Arun.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;Over time, Baldera fell into complete obscurity, witnessing tragedy after tragedy while completely shielded off from said dangers...</Page>
<Page social="0" voiceTypeId="0">After Tithus became the head the gods through brutality and ruthlessness, he continued down the same path and applied the same methods in governing Arborea.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;The Giants, which Tithus loved and sided with, slowly became just as brutal and ruthless like their god.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;By using Lok’s creation, Yurian caused the sun to go amok, and in one night’s time engulfed three major cities of the Holy Empire in a sea of fire. This incident will later be known as 'Day of Flame'&lt;BR&gt;Shakan, Velik, Kaia, Zenobia, Bahaar, and Ishara joined Yurian in his campaign against Tithus.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;Second divine war broke out because of this incident.</Page>
<Page social="0" voiceTypeId="0">Ah! This picturesque Balderan ridge!&lt;BR&gt;This magnificent and detailed architecture! A truly magnificent place.</Page>
<Page social="0" voiceTypeId="0">Akasha deceived us and poisoned the spring.</Page>
<Page social="0" voiceTypeId="0">Baldera is a utopia for ecologists.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;It's incredibly interesting to watch how a previously shielded ecosystem will change, don't you think? That's exactly what my heart feels.</Page>
<Page social="0" voiceTypeId="0">Baldera is such a fascinating place, is it not?&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;It's interesting to watch how it has changed after the barrier fell. What do you think, outsider?</Page>
<Page social="0" voiceTypeId="0">Balderon holds many secrets. Continue your investigation.&lt;CLOSEBUTTON&gt;</Page>
