<Page social="0" voiceTypeId="0">Cursed to a never-ending eternity until Balder returns, the Baraka have amassed centuries of knowledge and records between them. However, not all people of Arborea found this to be a "curse". The Enlightened Union of Allemantheia quickly sent envoys to assist in the creation of Balderon. The city began to flourish with their help, much to the dismay of the Free Traders Collective and the Valkyon Federation─ the sworn protectors and forebearers of Southern Arun.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;As the Enlightened Union assisted the Baraka of Baldera, they bartered with knowledge rather than gold. They provided their manpower to create architecture and guard researchers against the monsters of the Forest of Souls and Renegade Garden. Over time, notoriety spread through the world about the amount of knowledge that was now open to anyone willing to walk the path of peace.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;Tensions flared between the Enlightened Union and the Free Traders Collective, sparking battles and wars across Arborea. During this time, the Enlightened Union drew back their envoys to not bring war to Baldera's soil. As a final farewell, they left Baldera with one final gift─ a great barrier that would protect the region from the outside dangers for all of perpetuity. This barrier shielded all of Baldera like a time capsule to the outside world.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;Within the barrier however, things were not as they seemed... The Baraka began to notice Argonomorphs within their barrier. This caused those living in Baldera to begin training guard, going against their sworn path of peace, to protect the lives of those becoming trapped within their own shield.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;BR&gt;It seems that the Baraka too cannot escape the fate that befalls all of Arborea.</Page>
